{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/456851-golden-savanna-a-setting-for-demon-including-new-cryptoflora","id":456851,"title":"Golden Savanna - A setting for Demon, including new cryptoflora","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-25T07:56:02-07:00","id":456851,"title":"Golden Savanna - A setting for Demon, including new cryptoflora","content":"Six months ago, I wrote up this setting and sent it in for the open call for writers. Since I never heard back from them, I reasoned that this one probably didn't catch their attention. I liked it enough, though, that I thought I'd put it up here so that other Demon Storytellers might get a little use out of it. Enjoy!<br /> <br /> Golden Savanna<br /> <br /> On its surface, the Golden Savanna Retirement Village is no different than countless other gated communities dotting the face of suburbia. Dozens of identically bland houses populate a bewildering maze of streets and cul-de-sacs interspersed with numerous retention ponds. The Clubhouse combines a fitness center, a banquet hall, and a lounge into one convenient location for recreation and social interaction. Basic shopping needs are fulfilled by the convenience store, while a shuttle bus gives residents ready access to the nearby city. A chain link fence borders the perimeter of the village, broken only by a single gateway watched over by an ever-changing roster of bored security guards. The landscaping, consisting of colorful flowerbeds facing the external roads and extensive savanna surrounding the retention ponds, is lovely enough, though not truly remarkable.<br /> <br /> Demons know better. Everything seems too perfect. None of the residents have anything but good things to say about their home, but they are always telling the exact same stories about the place, as though the events occurred only yesterday. No family members ever visit, but the residents don\u2019t seem to notice. Despite their advanced ages, all the residents are in perfect health. Nobody is ever rushed to the hospital, and there hasn\u2019t been a death in years. Every Friday at exactly 10:42 P.M., a strange energy pulse flows out from the center of the community. The local Agency hasn\u2019t figured out the Infrastructure\u2019s purpose yet, but it suspects that it is something major.<br /> <br /> Senectus, the angel of Golden Savanna, has a plan. He oversaw the construction of the roads, warping space to make a labyrinth for his targets. He ensures that MacArthur Brothers Landscaping pays daily visits to the community, inoculating the soil with cryptoflora under the guise of fertilizer and weed treatments. The weekly energy pulse is nothing more than a lure. Golden Savanna is a Venus flytrap for demons. Senectus is just waiting for them to enter.<br /> <br /> Cryptoflora<br /> <br /> Vector Spores<br /> <br /> These fungal spores have been altered by exposure to the God Machine for the express purpose of creating new cryptoflora. When carried into the soil by water, these spores will connect to other fungal organisms they encounter, and spread the infection into them. When encountering mycorrhizal fungi, the infection will spread through the fungus into the host plant. It takes one week for each level of Size the host plant possesses for the infection to take full effect, at which point the plant becomes a Zoetic.<br /> <br /> Zoetics<br /> <br /> A Zoetic is a plant that has been infused by Vector Spores. This has given the plants a hunger for Aether and the capabilities to obtain it. Whenever a demon steps into an area overgrown with Zoetics, the plants animate, attempting to immobilize the demon so that they can feed upon it. The plants do not strategize and have no sense of self-preservation. They will always attempt to grapple their target, and always act last in combat. Zoetics are still rooted to the ground, and cannot give chase if a demon manages to escape them. Different types of Zoetics have different effects, depending on the host plant that has become infected, though all Zoetics have the Aether Eater Adaptation. Grasses and trees are the most common plants at Golden Savanna.<br /> <br /> Grasses: An individual grass is not particularly strong and has little chance of holding a struggling demon. The strength of grasses comes in their collective efforts. When moving through tall Zoetic grasses, a demon suffers the full effects of the Thicket Tilt (see below). If a character suffers the Knocked Down Tilt, he will also incur the Immobilized Tilt. When attempting to grapple a demon or keep one Immobilized, the collective Strength of tall grasses is considered to be 4. A character Immobilized by the grasses is considered to have both their legs and arms bound. Short grasses, such as those in a mown lawn, are far less dangerous. They do not cause the Thicket Tilt, but will inflict a -1 penalty to all physical rolls as they try to grab the demon\u2019s feet. A dramatic failure on any physical action in short Zoetic grasses will still cause the Knocked Down Tilt.<br /> <br /> Trees: Trees are generally much more dangerous on an individual basis, given their greater Size and Durability. Zoetic trees are considered to have a Strength score equal to their Size. They do not cause the Thicket Tilt unless they are growing very closely together, such as in a hedgerow.<br /> <br /> New Tilt<br /> <br /> Thicket (Environmental)<br /> Dense vegetation impedes the character\u2019s progress. Branches bar attempts to move forward, while vines entangle limbs and thorns scratch at any exposed surface. <br /> Effect: Trying to move through the dense vegetation is a challenge. All physical actions suffer a -2 penalty while entangled in the vegetation. A character\u2019s Speed is divided in half when attempting to walk, and attempting to run requires a Dexterity + Athletics roll. Success incurs only a level of Bashing damage each turn it is attempted, while failure additionally causes the Knocked Down Tilt as the character\u2019s feet are caught by the branches or vines beneath them. A dramatic failure on any other physical actions will also cause the Knocked Down Tilt. An additional point of bashing damage is caused each turn if the vegetation consists of thorns, unless the character is wearing suitably protective clothing. Perception rolls also receive a -3 penalty for vision, which also applies to hearing if the character is attempting to run. <br /> Causing the Tilt: Without supernatural powers, this Tilt is dependent on the natural growth of vegetation and cannot be caused by a character, though a clever one may be able to lead an opponent into an area where the Tilt would be incurred naturally. <br /> Ending the Tilt: The easiest way to end this Tilt is to move out of the area. At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, one or more turns spent actively clearing the area with appropriate equipment (such as a machete or chainsaw) may end this Tilt or prevent it entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:"